The derivation is confined to the Android sources, and specifically to:

  * the rounded-rect signed-distance decomposition into `radiusAt`,
    `sdRoundedRect` and `gradSdRoundedRect`, selected by a packed `float4` of
    per-corner radii
    — backdrop/src/commonMain/kotlin/com/kyant/backdrop/internal/Shaders.kt:22-48
  * the `uniform float2 size` / `uniform float2 offset` device-pixel framing and
    the `centered = (coord + offset) - halfSize` line
    — internal/Shaders.kt:54-55, :69 and effects/Lens.kt:45-46
  * the padding budget threaded through the effect chain
    — effects/Lens.kt:25-27, effects/Blur.kt:16-20
  * the "one cached RuntimeShader per shader-source variant" pattern
    — effects/Lens.kt:35-43
  * the highlight's angular falloff model, `pow(abs(dot(normal, lightDir)),
    falloff)` — internal/Shaders.kt:161-181 (`DefaultHighlightShaderString`)
  * the `interactive` press model (flat additive wash plus a radial lobe at the
    touch point, spring-driven) — the catalog app's InteractiveHighlight.kt
  * the example app's playground wallpaper,
    `example/assets/wallpaper-light.webp`, copied from
    app/src/commonMain/composeResources/drawable/wallpaper_light.webp. The
    AndroidLiquidGlass repository ships it uncredited; it appears to be an
    Apple iPhone stock wallpaper, is used here only as a development-time demo
    backdrop, and is excluded from the published npm package.

All refraction, chromatic-dispersion, tone and noise mathematics in
`GlassShaderSource.kt` is a translation of this project's own Metal shader,
`ios/Shaders/LiquidGlass.metal`. No AndroidLiquidGlass source is redistributed
and no binary dependency on it is declared.
